# Your USE flags: files here are yours, named as you like, and any line in
# them wins over the OS's defaults. Those are in /etc/portage/profile/package.use
# (Google's flags for the OS's packages, NickelOS's exceptions, and the flags
# each of Gentoo's packages in the OS was built with), which Portage reads
# first, as it reads a profile. Changing an OS package's flags rebuilds it
# for you (emerge --newuse); the OS itself is never changed.
